<%# Dev-only mock sign-in (story 0021). Real layout — this is an internal
    tool page, not the auth sheet, so there's no reason to strip chrome. %>
<h1>Sign in as…</h1>
<p>Local-only mock identity. Submitting flips <code>OmniAuth.config.test_mode</code>
  on for the rest of this server process — see the terminal if a later real
  sign-in unexpectedly behaves like this one.</p>

<%# `data: { turbo: false }` — code review (story 0021): Turbo Drive is pinned
    and imported globally (config/importmap.rb, the default layout). It
    intercepts non-GET form submissions and requires either a redirect or a
    turbo-stream response; `#create`'s happy path renders a plain 200 HTML
    page (the next auto-submit frame), which Turbo refuses to render for a
    form it intercepted ("Form responses must redirect to another
    location"). Without this, the door is inert in a real browser even
    though curl (no JS engine) never notices — that's exactly how the first
    version of this shipped broken. %>
<%= form_with url: dev_sign_in_submit_path, method: :post, data: { turbo: false } do |f| %>
  <div>
    <%= f.label :provider %>
    <%= f.select :provider, DevSessionsController::PROVIDERS %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <%= f.label :uid %>
    <%= f.text_field :uid, value: DevSessionsController::DEFAULT_UID %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <%= f.label :email %>
    <%= f.text_field :email, value: "dev@example.com" %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <%= f.label :name %>
    <%= f.text_field :name, value: "Dev Reader" %>
  </div>
  <%= f.submit "Sign in" %>
<% end %>
